  "title": "Debra B NDE 4516",
  "date": "'April 23, 2005'",
  "content": "I don't remember anything before the accident, as me and my ex-boyfriend were drinking heavily. All I know is it happened around 3:00 a.m. and the next thing I know, I feel this floating sensation - I wasn't in my body. Next, it was really dark, like a tunnel floating toward this light and as I was floating further on the light was getting bigger and brighter. Next, I saw my mom (she died in 2000) and she was standing in front of the light. She was wearing this white gown and it looked as if she was glowing. She had her head down and her eyes up staring at me and we were communicating in our minds. It was as if we could read each other's thoughts! I don't remember what we talked about, but I still remember what she looked like and that stare - the stare she always had when she was alive and worried about something. I was in a coma for a month, but it didn't feel that long at all in my NDE. It felt like maybe an hour or less, which tells me time doesn't exist in the afterlife!",
